# OpenRGB Sync plugin: per-zone LED count overrides.
#
# Copied to $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/aphotic-plugins/openrgb/zones.conf on first
# run (never overwritten again once it exists). Normally you don't hand
# edit this -- run scripts/setup.sh, which walks you through it and
# writes these lines for you. Safe to edit directly too.
#
# Format (colon-separated):
#   <case-insensitive substring of device name>:<zone index>:<led count>
#
# Zone index is 0-based, in the order `scripts/rgb_sync.py devices` lists
# a device's zones. This exists because controller-style hubs (Corsair
# Commander/Lighting Node, Lian Li Uni Hub fan hubs, and similar) report
# 0 LEDs until told how many are actually wired to each channel --
# OpenRGB cannot autodetect this for non-addressable/hub-style channels,
# and a zone at the wrong size silently ignores or misdistributes color.
#
# Sizes here are reasserted on every apply, not just at setup: an OpenRGB
# restart can bring a zone back at a stale nonzero size, which is exactly
# the case a "only fix zones reporting 0" check silently skips.
#
# Example, for a Corsair Commander Pro with a waterblock on channel 1
# (4 LEDs) and 3 fans (16 LEDs each = 48) on channel 2:
#
# Corsair Commander:0:4
# Corsair Commander:1:48
